WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.939
Why exactly one?

00:00:01.939 --> 00:00:05.784
Can a Legendre mode exceed one in absolute value?

00:00:06.114 --> 00:00:08.259
Every phase has modulus one.

00:00:08.259 --> 00:00:11.234
Each carries a positive weight, in every degree.

00:00:11.564 --> 00:00:13.877
Normalization gives the total weight.

00:00:13.877 --> 00:00:16.596
At angle zero, all phases equal one.

00:00:16.596 --> 00:00:19.267
The weights sum to P sub n of one, which is one.

00:00:19.597 --> 00:00:21.092
The disk is convex.

00:00:21.092 --> 00:00:26.084
It contains every weighted mean of these points, so the absolute value is at most one.

00:00:26.414 --> 00:00:28.601
The bound covers the whole interval.

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:32.899
Every x from minus one to one is cosine t for some angle.

00:00:33.229 --> 00:00:35.919
Now line up the phases at angle zero.

00:00:35.919 --> 00:00:38.395
The mean reaches one at the right endpoint.

00:00:38.395 --> 00:00:41.254
The supremum is exactly one, in every degree.

